# L §2.4 Values, §3.2 (tally 2.1.7 B3, issue #151; F21): a message names a price keyed by unit by the key's
# unit, PLN/fa, for a place of any unit the first its legs bring. 2.1.6's refcore printed the placeholder,
# `PLN/$u, not EUR/$u`. (T's G14 p130_one_kp with c_eur.)
=== p130_one_kp.tally
model kp
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "G14 probes for #130: per-unit prices keyed by a unit kind, by a clause and by a by"

source card "probe card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind funds: unit

kind ikes: place any min 0

kind pikes: place any min 0 priced px

kind wikes: place any min 0 priced qx

kind lots: place one min 0 priced px

kind unit_buys: event certain
  leg units: funds

place ike: ikes lives 2026-01-01..

place pike: pikes lives 2026-01-01..

place wike: wikes lives 2026-01-01..

place lot: lots fa lives 2026-01-01..

place market: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input px[u in funds]: num PLN/u

input qx[u in funds]: num PLN/fa

input pl[u in funds]: num PLN/u reading

input buy_day: date

input n3a: num fa

input n2b: num fb

input n5a: num fa

move b1: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to ike amount n3a

move b2: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to ike amount n2b

move b3: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to pike amount n3a

move b4: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to pike amount n2b

move b5: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to wike amount n2b

move b6: unit_buys
  on buy_day
  leg units from market to lot amount n5a

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  funds + [fa] lives 2026-01-01..
  funds + [fb] lives 2026-01-01..
  buy_day = 2026-02-10 "the card"
  n3a = 3 fa "the card"
  n2b = 2 fb "the card"
  n5a = 5 fa "the card"
  px[fa] = 10 PLN/fa "the card"
  px[fb] = 20 PLN/fb "the card"
  qx[fa] = 7 PLN/fa "the card"
  qx[fb] = 9 PLN/fa "the card"

version readings_2026
  cite card
  governs 2026-01..2026-12
  known 2026-01-01
  pl[fa] = 11 PLN/fa at 2026-03-01 "quoted"
  pl[fb] = 21 PLN/fb at 2026-03-01 "quoted"
=== p130_one_c_eur.tally
part p_c_eur
  tally 2

ask c_eur: value(pike, 2026-03-31) in EUR
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT value(pike) in EUR: pike is priced in PLN/fa, not EUR/fa ...
